  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::feedbackUI
  feedbackCanvas: {fileID: 201115860}
  txtFeedback: {fileID: 414145330}
  sceneFeedbacks:
  - sceneName: 2a_leavingCar
    goodRequiredActions:
    - vest
    - hazardLight
    mediumRequiredActions:
    - tlf
    goodText: Good preparation.\nTurning on hazard lights and wearing a high-visibility
      vest are crucial for your safety and to warn other drivers. Securing the car
      is also important before leaving it.\n
    mediumText: Before calling emergency services, you should assess the situation
      to provide accurate information.
    badText: Before leaving your vehicle, you must secure the situation. Hazard lights
      and a high-visibility vest are essential to avoid further danger. Always ensure
      your own safety before helping others.\n
  - sceneName: 2b_bringFromCar
    goodRequiredActions:
    - triangle
    mediumRequiredActions:
    - firstAidKit
    goodText: Good decision.\nBringing a warning triangle is essential to alert other
      drivers and prevent further accidents.  Securing the scene is the first priority
      before approaching the situation.\n
    mediumText: Bringing first aid equipment can be helpful if someone is injured. 
      However, securing the scene should always come before providing assistance.
    badText: This is not safe.\nYou did not bring a warning triangle.  Without proper
      warning, other drivers may not see the accident in time, increasing the risk
      of further collisions.  Always secure the scene before approaching.\n
  - sceneName: 3A
    goodRequiredActions:
    - triangle
    mediumRequiredActions: []
    goodText: Good decision.\nYou secured the scene and checked for potential hazards
      before approaching. This reduces risk and ensures your safety.
    mediumText: 
    badText: "This is not safe.\\nYou approached the vehicle without securing the
      scene. Placing a warning triangle is essential to warn other drivers and prevent
      further accidents.\\n\\nGame Over \u2013 you did not ensure a safe approach."
